        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ದುಡಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದುಡಿ — duḍi — \"to toil; to labour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕುಟುಂಬಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಅಪ್ಪ ಹಗಲು ರಾತ್ರಿ ದುಡಿದರು. kuṭumbakkāgi appa hagalu rātri duḍidaru. Father toiled day and night for the family."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ದುಡಿದೆ, duḍide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದುಡಿಮೆ is the work and what it earns."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದುಡಿ (duḍi) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3295 lists Kannada duḍi, \"to labour, acquire by one's labour\", and duḍime, \"gain\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
